\subsubsection{Representation-Space Sensitivity in NORA and Reference VLMs}
\label{sec:cf_repr}

NORA and action-untrained reference VLMs require representation-space metrics and are therefore reported separately.
These values should be interpreted as auxiliary evidence of representational sensitivity rather than direct action-space effect sizes.
NORA Goal produces saturated exit-layer cosine distances of $1.0$ for all conditions; NORA Spatial yields a peak cosine distance of $0.275$.
Reference VLMs show weak sensitivity: the TracVLA reference (Phi-3-Vision) produces peak cosine distances of $0.15$--$0.19$; the NORA reference (Qwen2.5-VL) yields $0.081$ on Goal (see Appendix~\ref{sec:cf_details_appendix} for metric discussion).

tool_args.new_string:
\subsubsection{Representation-Space Sensitivity in NORA and Reference VLMs}
\label{sec:cf_repr}

NORA and action-untrained reference VLMs lack action outputs; their sensitivity is measured via cosine distance on hidden representations, which operates on a different scale from Cohen's $d$ and should be interpreted as auxiliary evidence.
NORA Goal produces saturated cosine distances ($1.0$); NORA Spatial peaks at $0.275$.
Reference VLMs show weak sensitivity ($\leq 0.19$; Appendix~\ref{sec:cf_details_appendix}).

\paragraph{Synthesis.}
Training-associated effects concentrate at the readout token ($+0.069$ $R^2$ shift vs.\ $+0.015$ at image\_mean), while L1 instruction attention is inherited from base-model pretraining (Phi-3-Vision: 32/32, Qwen2.5-VL: 13--14/16 before training).
Mid-layer probes outperform exit-layer probes in architectures with pronounced collapse, suggesting potential early-exit efficiency gains ($\rho = 0.583$, $p = 0.10$; Appendix~\ref{sec:extended_discussion_appendix}).

